,title,link,text,language,family
0,Kua-nsi language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kua-nsi_language,"Kua-nsi (kʰua33 n̩21 sɨ55; Chinese: 跨恩斯话; Hedong Yi 河东彝) is a Loloish language of Heqing County, Yunnan, China. Gomotage (ɣɔ21 mɔ33 ta55 ɣə21), an undocumented and little-known Loloish language of Eryuan County, is also probably related to Kua-nsi (Yang 2010:7).",Kua-nsi,Sino-Tibetan
1,Music of Tibet - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Tibet,"May 6, 2026 - The music of Tibet reflects the cultural heritage of the trans-Himalayan region centered in Tibet, but also known wherever Indigenous Tibetan groups are found in Nepal, Bhutan, India and further abroad. The religious music of Tibet reflects the profound influence of Tibetan Buddhism on the culture.",Kua-nsi,Sino-Tibetan
2,Tibetan Music | Himalayan Temple | Instrumental Asian Music,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J9dAmDy3jWE,"Relaxing music for listening while you work, study, read, relax or sleep. From world music to instrumental piano and lofi/chill.",Kua-nsi,Sino-Tibetan
3,Kua-nsi language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/kua_nsi_language,"Kua-nsi (also known as Kua'nsi or Hedong Yi) is a Central Ngwi (Loloish) language of the Sino-Tibetan family, spoken by approximately 5,000 people primarily in seven villages of Liuhe Township, Heqing County, Dali Bai Autonomous Prefecture, Yunnan Province, China. [1] [2] The language serves as the main medium of communication within homogeneous Kua-nsi communities, where speakers are ...",Kua-nsi,Sino-Tibetan
