5,"Tibetan Music & Audio — Stream & Download Traditional Music, Chants ...",https://www.tibetanlibrary.com/collections/audio,"Listen to and download free Tibetan music, sacred chants, mantras, dharma teachings, folk songs, and oral histories. Stream rare recordings of traditional Tibetan instruments, monastic chanting, and contemporary Tibetan artists.",Kua-nsi,Sino-Tibetan
6,Kua-nsi in China people group profile | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/20588/CH,"The Kua-nsi people, a small ethnic group in China, reside in the southwestern region of Yunnan Province. Their origins are closely tied to the larger Tibeto-Burman language family, though the Kua-nsi have developed a distinct identity through centuries of isolation in the mountainous terrain.",Kua-nsi,Sino-Tibetan
7,Sino-Tibetan | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/236/,"Kua-nsi ykn, a language of China · Kuamasi yku, a language of China · Laghuu lgh, a language of Viet Nam · Mantsi nty, a language of Viet Nam · Moji ymi, a language of China · Muji, Northern ymx, a language of China · Muji, Qila ymq, a language of China ·",Kua-nsi,Sino-Tibetan
8,MUSIC IN TIBET | Facts and Details,https://factsanddetails.com/china/cat6/sub36/item206.html,Their songs and music are well-modulated in tone and the words fit well with the tunes.The areas inhabited by Tibetans boasts a great diversity of folk songs and dances. Some musical instruments were introduced from the interior of China.,Kua-nsi,Sino-Tibetan
